        "original_id": "ffe761f2-0d9e-5c1a-ba85-9a4444e8286c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ferrari 360, Ferrari F355, Porsche 911, Lamborghini Diablo, Mitsubishi Lancer, Subaru Impreza, HSV\n- Companies: Ferrari, PROCAR\n- Organizations: Australian Nations Cup Championship, Australian GT Production Car Championship, Mille Miglia\n- People: Vittorio Colocci\n- Concepts: sports cars, GT cars, racing series\n\nFacts:\n- Vittorio Colocci entered 15 races between 1950 and 1956, including four editions of the Mille Miglia, mainly driving Ferraris and Lancias.\n- Vittorio Colocci achieved one class victory and two second-place finishes among his best results.\n- Ferrari built the Ferrari F355 sports car, also known as Type F129, from May 1994 to 1999.\n- In 2000, PROCAR split the Australian GT Production Car Championship into the new Australian Nations Cup Championship and a revised Australian GT Production Car Championship.\n- In 2000, exotic GT cars such as the Porsche 911, Ferrari 360, and Lamborghini Diablo competed in the Australian Nations Cup Championship.\n- In 2000, lesser vehicles such as the Mitsubishi Lancer, Subaru Impreza, and HSV competed for outright wins in the revised Australian GT Production Car Championship.\n- Ferrari built the Ferrari 360 as a two-seater sports car from 1999 to 2005.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3700ab5f-a3d0-5c13-aac3-235532365b95",
        "text": "Page: Ferrari 360. Sentence: The Ferrari 360 is a two-seater sports car built by Ferrari from 1999 to 2005.\nPage: Ferrari F355. Sentence: The Ferrari F355 (Type F129) is a sports car built by Ferrari from May 1994 to 1999.\nPage: Australian Nations Cup Championship. Sentence: For 2000, PROCAR split the Australian GT Production Car Championship into two separate series so that the more exotic GT cars such as Porsche 911s, Ferrari 360s and Lamborghini Diablo's could compete in the new Australian Nations Cup Championship and the lesser vehicles such as the Mitsubishi Lancers, Subaru Imprezas and HSV's could now compete for outright wins in the revised Australian GT Production Car Championship.\nPage: Vittorio Colocci. Sentence: He entered 15 races between 1950 and 1956, including four times the Mille Miglia, mainly driving Ferraris and Lancias. His best results include one class victory and two second places.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
